Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Meridian: Improve with AI finds Claude Code in every
 space

The boost editor asked the active tab's profile for the AI, so in a space
with its own profile it said "Set up an AI in Settings"; it now asks the
main profile, as Improve does. "Automatic" (nothing picked in Settings > AI)
now also falls back to the first agent found on this computer (Claude Code
first; opt-in ones only with Other agents on), from the cached detection.
Improve runs as the space's AI account, like Ask.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
